  The game changes once you wake up Rodney.  You have some place
to go and the quicker you get there the better.  Unnecessary 
fighting wastes time that could be better spent traveling, and
lets more monsters try to mob you.  With wands of teleport,
almost all fighting is unnecessary.

  When you do have to fight, instakills are the way to go.
(Hint: what does everyone want to get from Orcus?)


  You should be traveling as fast as possible on the Astral 
Planes.  Note: traveling, not necessarily just moving.  
The only time you stop moving is when monsters are blocking you
completely.  Then you generally zap a wand of teleport and carry
on.

  What you want most on the Ascension run is to be *left alone*.
Ring of conflict will do this, and may well cause more damage
than anything else in the game.  Being invisible/displaced helps
as well.  (And displacement can be very entertaining.)

  Get mobbed five deep in the middle of the Plane of Air and no
weapon can save you.  Possibly not even Skilled+ XL 30 cone of
cold or fireball.  And while you're busy fighting, more monsters
will be showing up.  Keep moving and remember the first rule
of bad driving:  "What is in your rear view mirror does not 
count."

  Most of the escape methods you use in the Dungeons of Doom et.
al. will not work on the Planes.  E.g.  

  - Cursed/confused scroll of teleportation.
  - Teleportitis
  - Cursed potion of gain level
  - Wands of fire/lightning can't write a permanent Elbereth 
    on the Planes of Air or Water.
  - Immediately going back up the stairs.
  - Wand of digging downward.
  - Scrolls of earth don't work on *any* of the Astral Planes.
  - Porting with the Eye of Aethiopica (Well, I don't think so.)
  - Level porting with the Orb of Fate
  - etc.
  - Nor can you go back to your stash to get something.
 

  You're *fleeing forward*.  All you can depend on having is what
you carry with you.  Anything you leave behind in the Dungeons is
as inaccessible as if it had been totally  destroyed.

  The usual "melee, then escape if warranted" approach is 
unsuitable.  And the lava and water can be an instadeath on
the Planes of Fire and Water.

  So remember, players have ascended without killing anything at
any time.  Trying to emulate a pacifist can let you travel much
faster.  Don't hesitate to kill when necessary, though.

>I currently have magic resistance through a gray dragon scale mail
>as well as through Magicbane, and I have reflection through an
>amulet.

  Looks good.  Magicbane's curse resistance will also help a lot.
You can reduce the amount of holy water, b?oRC, wands of 
cancellation, etc. you carry on the Run.  NB: Reduce, not 
eliminate.

  Magicbane is only 95% effective at nullifying curses.  And you
may lose it.  NB: Spell of remove curse and spell of cancellation
are *wonderful* emergency backups.  No weight.  

  Spell of cancellation even at 50% failure can be well worth it 
with a cursed bag of holding.  No chance of a magical explosion 
either.

  Silver dragon scale mail and CoMR permits wearing an amulet of
life saving.  Tough to lose the CoMR, and you'll still have 
wielded Magicbane as backup Magic Resistance.  (Playing a wizard
gives MR from the Eye of Aethiopica as well.  And, yes, I use
all three of them.)


  Amulets of life saving can greatly improve the "learn by dying"
experience on the Ascension run.  One guaranteed amulet of life 
saving in Vlad's Tower.  Get more by polying other amulets found 
(uncurse them first, if you don't bless them.)

  Much easier, and more satisfying, to learn from a death during
the Ascension Run if an amulet of life saving lets you apply that
lesson immediately.

  (Someone on the plane of water was wearing an amulet of magical
breathing while *in* the water.  He put on a ring of levitation,
then removed the "oMB...and immediately drowned.  Apparently you
have to do '<' to rise above the water first, if you're in the
water.)

  So keep an eye out for Silver Dragons and a cloak of MR.  Don't
kill a silver dragon unless you have a means of reviving it.
(In case you don't get scales.)


